---
// src/pages/pension-calculator.astro
const siteUrl = "https://8paycommission.com";
const canonicalURL = new URL(Astro.url.pathname, siteUrl);
const pageTitle = "8th Pay Commission Pension Calculator: Expected Pension Hike, Family Pension & Commutation";
const pageDescription = "Calculate your projected 8th Central Pay Commission basic pension, family pension, commuted amount, and net in-hand pension hike with real-time arithmetic.";

// Pension benchmarks across pay matrix tiers
const pensionBenchmarks = [
  { level: "Level 1 (GP 1800)", post: "MTS / Group D", base7th: 18000, pension7th: 9000 },
  { level: "Level 2 (GP 1900)", post: "LDC / Junior Clerk", base7th: 19900, pension7th: 9950 },
  { level: "Level 3 (GP 2000)", post: "Constable / Driver", base7th: 21700, pension7th: 10850 },
  { level: "Level 4 (GP 2400)", post: "UDC / Head Constable", base7th: 25500, pension7th: 12750 },
  { level: "Level 5 (GP 2800)", post: "Auditor / Accountant", base7th: 29200, pension7th: 14600 },
  { level: "Level 6 (GP 4200)", post: "Inspector / Sub-Inspector", base7th: 35400, pension7th: 17700 },
  { level: "Level 7 (GP 4600)", post: "ASO / Section Engineer", base7th: 44900, pension7th: 22450 },
  { level: "Level 8 (GP 4800)", post: "AAO / Section Officer", base7th: 47600, pension7th: 23800 },
  { level: "Level 9 (GP 5400)", post: "Senior Accounts Officer", base7th: 53100, pension7th: 26550 },
  { level: "Level 10 (GP 5400)", post: "Group A Entry / SDM / DSP", base7th: 56100, pension7th: 28050 },
  { level: "Level 11 (GP 6600)", post: "Under Secretary / Exec Engineer", base7th: 67700, pension7th: 33850 },
  { level: "Level 12 (GP 7600)", post: "Deputy Secretary / SE", base7th: 78800, pension7th: 39400 },
  { level: "Level 13 (GP 8700)", post: "Director / Selection Grade", base7th: 123100, pension7th: 61550 },
  { level: "Level 14 (GP 10000)", post: "Joint Secretary / IG", base7th: 144200, pension7th: 72100 },
  { level: "Level 17 (Apex Scale)", post: "Secretary to Govt of India", base7th: 225000, pension7th: 112500 },
  { level: "Level 18 (Cabinet Sec)", post: "Cabinet Secretary of India", base7th: 250000, pension7th: 125000 }
];

const faqs = [
  {
    q: "How does the 8th Pay Commission pension calculator calculate revised pension?",
    a: "The calculator scales your current 7th CPC basic pension by the selected fitment multiplier (such as 2.25x or 2.86x). It then factors in your commuted pension portion, adds applicable age-based extra pension quantum (if aged 80 or above), and sets initial Dearness Relief (DR) to 0% to project your net monthly take-home pension."
  },
  {
    q: "What happens to Dearness Relief (DR) when the 8th Pay Commission is implemented?",
    a: "All accumulated Dearness Relief is absorbed directly into the basic pension via the fitment factor. Once implemented, DR resets to 0% and starts accumulating anew biannually based on the 12-month moving average of the All-India Consumer Price Index for Industrial Workers (AICPI-IW)."
  },
  {
    q: "How is Family Pension calculated under the 8th Central Pay Commission?",
    a: "Under standard Central Civil Services (Pension) Rules, normal family pension is pegged at 30% of the last drawn basic pay (or corresponding revised basic pay in the matrix), subject to the revised statutory minimum pension floor (which rises from ₹9,000 to approximately ₹20,250 – ₹25,740 depending on the fitment factor)."
  },
  {
    q: "What is the key demand regarding the commuted pension restoration period?",
    a: "Central government pensioner associations and staff side federations have submitted representations requesting the commutation recovery period be reduced from 15 years to 12 years. The rationale is that the commuted capital along with nominal interest is fully recovered within 11 to 12 years under prevailing interest rates."
  },
  {
    q: "Are defence veterans and civilian pensioners treated equally under the 8th CPC?",
    a: "Yes, basic pension calculations utilize the identical fitment factor to ensure parity. However, armed forces veterans also receive revisions to Military Service Pay (MSP), which factors into pension calculations for qualifying service cadres."
  }
];
---

<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8" />
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0, maximum-scale=5.0" />
  <title>{pageTitle}</title>
  <meta name="description" content={pageDescription} />
  <meta name="keywords" content="8th pay commission pension calculator, 8th cpc pension hike, family pension calculator, commutation restoration, central government pensioners, dear relief reset" />
  <meta name="robots" content="index, follow, max-snippet:-1, max-image-preview:large" />
  <link rel="canonical" href={canonicalURL} />

  <!-- Open Graph -->
  <meta property="og:locale" content="en_IN" />
  <meta property="og:type" content="website" />
  <meta property="og:title" content={pageTitle} />
  <meta property="og:description" content={pageDescription} />
  <meta property="og:url" content={canonicalURL} />
  <meta property="og:site_name" content="8th Pay Commission Portal" />

  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com" />
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin />
  <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Plus+Jakarta+Sans:wght@400;500;600;700;800&display=swap" rel="stylesheet" />

  <!-- Schema.org WebApplication + FAQPage -->
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify({
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@graph": [
      {
        "@type": "WebApplication",
        "name": "8th Pay Commission Pension Calculator",
        "url": canonicalURL.toString(),
        "operatingSystem": "All",
        "applicationCategory": "FinanceApplication",
        "offers": { "@type": "Offer", "price": "0", "priceCurrency": "INR" }
      },
      {
        "@type": "FAQPage",
        "mainEntity": faqs.map((f) => ({
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": f.q,
          "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": f.a }
        }))
      }
    ]
  })} />

  <style>
    :root {
      --bg: #f8fafc;
      --surface: #ffffff;
      --surface-subtle: #f1f5f9;
      --border: #e2e8f0;
      --primary: #1d4ed8;
      --primary-hover: #1e40af;
      --primary-gradient: linear-gradient(135deg, #1d4ed8 0%, #0284c7 100%);
      --text: #0f172a;
      --text-muted: #64748b;
      --accent-green: #15803d;
      --accent-green-bg: #dcfce7;
      --radius-sm: 8px;
      --radius-md: 14px;
      --radius-lg: 20px;
      --shadow-sm: 0 1px 3px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.05);
      --shadow-md: 0 4px 12px -2px rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.08);
      --shadow-lg: 0 16px 32px -4px rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.08);
    }

    * { box-sizing: border-box; margin: 0; padding: 0; font-family: 'Plus Jakarta Sans', system-ui, sans-serif; }
    body { background: var(--bg); color: var(--text); line-height: 1.7; font-size: 15px; -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased; }
    a { color: var(--primary); text-decoration: none; transition: color 0.2s ease; }
    a:hover { color: var(--primary-hover); }

    .layout-wrap { max-width: 1100px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 0 1.25rem; }

    /* Hero Header */
    .hero-header {
      text-align: center;
      padding: 3rem 1rem 1.75rem;
    }
    .badge-pill {
      display: inline-flex;
      align-items: center;
      gap: 0.4rem;
      background: #eff6ff;
      border: 1px solid #bfdbfe;
      color: #1d4ed8;
      padding: 0.25rem 0.85rem;
      border-radius: 30px;
      font-size: 0.78rem;
      font-weight: 700;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      letter-spacing: 0.05em;
      margin-bottom: 0.85rem;
    }
    .hero-header h1 {
      font-size: clamp(1.85rem, 4vw, 2.75rem);
      font-weight: 800;
      letter-spacing: -0.035em;
      line-height: 1.22;
      margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
      color: var(--text);
    }
    .hero-header p {
      color: var(--text-muted);
      max-width: 740px;
      margin: 0 auto;
      font-size: 1.05rem;
    }

    /* Calculator Widget Box */
    .calc-box {
      background: var(--surface);
      border: 1px solid var(--border);
      border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
      padding: 2rem;
      box-shadow: var(--shadow-lg);
      margin-bottom: 3.5rem;
    }
    .chip-bar {
      display: flex;
      gap: 0.5rem;
      overflow-x: auto;
      padding: 0.5rem 0 1.25rem;
      scrollbar-width: none;
    }
    .chip-bar::-webkit-scrollbar { display: none; }
    .chip-btn {
      background: #f1f5f9;
      border: 1px solid var(--border);
      color: #475569;
      padding: 0.5rem 1.1rem;
      border-radius: 30px;
      font-size: 0.84rem;
      font-weight: 700;
      white-space: nowrap;
      cursor: pointer;
      transition: all 0.15s ease;
    }
    .chip-btn:hover { background: #e2e8f0; }
    .chip-btn.active {
      background: var(--primary);
      border-color: var(--primary);
      color: #ffffff;
      box-shadow: 0 2px 8px rgba(29, 78, 216, 0.3);
    }

    .form-grid {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(220px, 1fr));
      gap: 1.25rem;
      margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
    }
    .form-item {
      display: flex;
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: 0.4rem;
    }
    .form-item label {
      font-size: 0.82rem;
      font-weight: 700;
      color: #334155;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      letter-spacing: 0.03em;
    }
    .form-item input, .form-item select {
      background: #ffffff;
      border: 1.5px solid #cbd5e1;
      color: var(--text);
      padding: 0.75rem 0.9rem;
      border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
      font-size: 0.96rem;
      font-weight: 600;
      outline: none;
      transition: all 0.2s;
    }
    .form-item input:focus, .form-item select:focus {
      border-color: var(--primary);
      box-shadow: 0 0 0 3px rgba(37, 99, 235, 0.15);
    }

    /* Live Summary Cards */
    .summary-cards {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(200px, 1fr));
      gap: 1rem;
      margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
    }
    .kpi-unit {
      background: #f8fafc;
      border: 1px solid var(--border);
      border-radius: var(--radius-md);
      padding: 1.25rem;
      text-align: center;
      position: relative;
    }
    .kpi-unit.highlight {
      background: #eff6ff;
      border-color: #bfdbfe;
    }
    .kpi-unit.success {
      background: var(--accent-green-bg);
      border-color: #86efac;
    }
    .kpi-unit .kpi-label {
      font-size: 0.75rem;
      font-weight: 700;
      color: var(--text-muted);
      text-transform: uppercase;
      margin-bottom: 0.35rem;
    }
    .kpi-unit .kpi-val {
      font-size: 1.5rem;
      font-weight: 800;
      color: var(--text);
    }
    .kpi-unit.highlight .kpi-val { color: var(--primary); }
    .kpi-unit.success .kpi-val { color: var(--accent-green); }

    /* Breakdown Slip */
    .breakdown-box {
      background: #f8fafc;
      border: 1px solid var(--border);
      border-radius: var(--radius-md);
      padding: 1.5rem;
      margin-top: 1.5rem;
    }
    .breakdown-title {
      font-weight: 800;
      font-size: 1rem;
      color: var(--text);
      margin-bottom: 0.85rem;
      display: flex;
      justify-content: space-between;
      align-items: center;
    }
    .breakdown-table {
      width: 100%;
      border-collapse: collapse;
      font-size: 0.94rem;
    }
    .breakdown-table td {
      padding: 0.65rem 0.5rem;
      border-bottom: 1px dashed #cbd5e1;
    }
    .breakdown-table tr:last-child td { border-bottom: none; }
    .breakdown-table td.num {
      text-align: right;
      font-weight: 700;
    }

    /* Content Area */
    .article-wrap {
      background: var(--surface);
      border: 1px solid var(--border);
      border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
      padding: 2.75rem;
      box-shadow: var(--shadow-sm);
      margin-bottom: 3.5rem;
    }
    .article-wrap h2 {
      font-size: 1.6rem;
      font-weight: 800;
      color: var(--text);
      letter-spacing: -0.025em;
      margin: 2.5rem 0 1rem;
      padding-bottom: 0.5rem;
      border-bottom: 2px solid #eff6ff;
    }
    .article-wrap h3 {
      font-size: 1.25rem;
      font-weight: 700;
      color: #1e293b;
      margin: 1.6rem 0 0.65rem;
    }
    .article-wrap p {
      margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
      color: #334155;
      font-size: 1.02rem;
    }
    .article-wrap ul, .article-wrap ol {
      margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
      padding-left: 1.5rem;
      color: #334155;
    }
    .article-wrap li { margin-bottom: 0.45rem; }

    .formula-banner {
      background: #eff6ff;
      border-left: 4px solid var(--primary);
      padding: 1.15rem 1.35rem;
      border-radius: 0 8px 8px 0;
      margin: 1.5rem 0;
      font-family: monospace;
      font-size: 0.96rem;
      color: #1e40af;
    }

    /* Table */
    .table-responsive {
      overflow-x: auto;
      border: 1px solid var(--border);
      border-radius: var(--radius-md);
      margin: 1.5rem 0;
    }
    table.data-table {
      width: 100%;
      border-collapse: collapse;
      text-align: left;
      font-size: 0.92rem;
    }
    table.data-table th, table.data-table td {
      padding: 0.85rem 1rem;
      border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    }
    table.data-table th {
      background: #f8fafc;
      color: #475569;
      font-weight: 700;
      font-size: 0.8rem;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      letter-spacing: 0.04em;
    }
    table.data-table tr:hover td { background: #f8fafc; }

    /* Level Badges */
    .level-grid {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(130px, 1fr));
      gap: 0.65rem;
      margin: 1.25rem 0;
    }
    .level-pill {
      background: #ffffff;
      border: 1px solid var(--border);
      padding: 0.75rem 0.5rem;
      border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
      text-align: center;
      cursor: pointer;
      transition: all 0.2s ease;
    }
    .level-pill:hover {
      border-color: var(--primary);
      transform: translateY(-2px);
      box-shadow: var(--shadow-md);
      background: #eff6ff;
    }
    .level-pill strong { display: block; font-size: 0.95rem; color: var(--text); }
    .level-pill span { font-size: 0.78rem; color: var(--text-muted); }

    /* FAQ */
    .faq-unit {
      border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
      padding: 1.15rem 0;
    }
    .faq-quest {
      font-weight: 700;
      color: var(--text);
      cursor: pointer;
      display: flex;
      justify-content: space-between;
      align-items: center;
      font-size: 1.02rem;
    }
    .faq-ans {
      display: none;
      padding-top: 0.65rem;
      color: #475569;
      font-size: 0.96rem;
      line-height: 1.7;
    }
    .faq-unit.open .faq-ans { display: block; }
    .faq-unit.open .faq-arrow { transform: rotate(180deg); }
    .faq-arrow { transition: transform 0.2s ease; font-size: 0.75rem; color: var(--text-muted); }

    /* Mobile Sticky Summary Bar */
    .mobile-sticky-bar {
      display: none;
      position: fixed;
      bottom: 0;
      left: 0;
      right: 0;
      background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.96);
      border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
      backdrop-filter: blur(12px);
      padding: 0.75rem 1.25rem;
      z-index: 990;
      justify-content: space-between;
      align-items: center;
      box-shadow: 0 -4px 16px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.06);
    }
    .mobile-sticky-bar .lbl { font-size: 0.74rem; color: var(--text-muted); text-transform: uppercase; font-weight: 700; }
    .mobile-sticky-bar .val { font-size: 1.2rem; font-weight: 800; color: var(--primary); }
    @media (max-width: 768px) {
      .mobile-sticky-bar { display: flex; }
      body { padding-bottom: 4.5rem; }
    }

    /* Minimal Bottom Disclaimers */
    .disclaimer-strip {
      max-width: 1100px;
      margin: 2rem auto 4rem;
      padding: 1.25rem;
      background: #f8fafc;
      border: 1px solid var(--border);
      border-left: 4px solid #94a3b8;
      border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
      font-size: 0.82rem;
      line-height: 1.6;
      color: #64748b;
    }
  </style>
</head>
<body>

  <main class="layout-wrap">

    <!-- HERO HEADER -->
    <header class="hero-header">
      <div class="badge-pill">Pensioner & Family Welfare Model (2026)</div>
      <h1>8th Pay Commission Pension Calculator</h1>
      <p>Estimate revised basic pension, family pension, commuted deductions, and additional age-based quantum for retired Central Government and Armed Forces personnel.</p>
    </header>

    <!-- INTERACTIVE PENSION CALCULATOR -->
    <section class="calc-box" aria-label="8th Pay Commission Pension Calculator Widget">
      
      <!-- Multiplier Pills -->
      <div style="margin-bottom: 1.25rem;">
        <span style="font-size: 0.8rem; font-weight: 700; color: #64748b; text-transform: uppercase;">Expected Fitment Factor:</span>
        <div class="chip-bar" id="factorPills">
          <button class="chip-btn" data-f="1.92">1.92x (Conservative)</button>
          <button class="chip-btn" data-f="2.25">2.25x (Baseline Model)</button>
          <button class="chip-btn" data-f="2.57">2.57x (7th CPC Parity)</button>
          <button class="chip-btn active" data-f="2.86">2.86x (Federation Target)</button>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Form Controls -->
      <div class="form-grid">
        <div class="form-item">
          <label for="pensionLevelSelect">Pay Level at Retirement</label>
          <select id="pensionLevelSelect">
            {pensionBenchmarks.map((item) => (
              <option value={item.pension7th} selected={item.level.startsWith("Level 6")}>
                {item.level} - Current Pension ₹{item.pension7th.toLocaleString('en-IN')}
              </option>
            ))}
          </select>
        </div>

        <div class="form-item">
          <label for="currentPensionInput">Current 7th CPC Basic Pension (₹)</label>
          <input type="number" id="currentPensionInput" value="17700" min="9000" step="50" />
        </div>

        <div class="form-item">
          <label for="fitmentSelect">Fitment Multiplier</label>
          <select id="fitmentSelect">
            <option value="1.92">1.92x (Conservative Baseline)</option>
            <option value="2.10">2.10x (Moderate)</option>
            <option value="2.25">2.25x (Consensus Projection)</option>
            <option value="2.57">2.57x (Equivalent to 7th CPC)</option>
            <option value="2.86" selected>2.86x (Federation Demand)</option>
            <option value="3.00">3.00x (High Demand)</option>
          </select>
        </div>

        <div class="form-item">
          <label for="commutationSelect">Commutation Status</label>
          <select id="commutationSelect">
            <option value="0">No Commutation (Full Pension)</option>
            <option value="0.20">20% Commuted</option>
            <option value="0.30">30% Commuted</option>
            <option value="0.40" selected>40% Commuted (Max Allowed)</option>
          </select>
        </div>

        <div class="form-item">
          <label for="ageQuantumSelect">Pensioner Age Bracket</label>
          <select id="ageQuantumSelect">
            <option value="0" selected>Under 80 Years (Normal Basic)</option>
            <option value="0.20">80 to 85 Years (+20% Additional)</option>
            <option value="0.30">85 to 90 Years (+30% Additional)</option>
            <option value="0.40">90 to 95 Years (+40% Additional)</option>
            <option value="0.50">95 to 100 Years (+50% Additional)</option>
            <option value="1.00">100 Years or More (+100% Additional)</option>
          </select>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Results KPI Grid -->
      <div class="summary-cards">
        <div class="kpi-unit">
          <div class="kpi-label">Revised Basic Pension</div>
          <div class="kpi-val" id="dispBasicPension">₹50,622</div>
        </div>
        <div class="kpi-unit highlight">
          <div class="kpi-label">Family Pension (30% Slabs)</div>
          <div class="kpi-val" id="dispFamilyPension">₹30,373</div>
        </div>
        <div class="kpi-unit success">
          <div class="kpi-label">Net Monthly Take-Home</div>
          <div class="kpi-val" id="dispNetPension">₹31,373</div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Live Pension Slip Breakdown -->
      <div class="breakdown-box">
        <div class="breakdown-title">
          <span>Projected Monthly Pension Disbursal Slip</span>
          <span style="color: var(--primary); font-size: 0.85rem;" id="slipTierLabel">Level 6 (GP 4200)</span>
        </div>
        <table class="breakdown-table">
          <tbody>
            <tr>
              <td>Revised 8th CPC Full Basic Pension (7th Pension × Fitment Factor)</td>
              <td class="num" id="slipFullBasic">₹50,622</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>Dearness Relief (DR) — <span style="color: var(--text-muted);">Reset to 0% at rollout</span></td>
              <td class="num">₹0</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>Additional Age Quantum (Enhanced Living Allowance for 80+ Years)</td>
              <td class="num" id="slipAgeQuantum">₹0</td>
            </tr>
            <tr style="font-weight: 700; background: #f8fafc;">
              <td>Total Gross Pension Entitlement</td>
              <td class="num" id="slipGrossPension" style="color: var(--primary);">₹50,622</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>Less: Commuted Pension Monthly Recovery Portion</td>
              <td class="num" id="slipCommutedDeduct" style="color: #dc2626;">-₹20,249</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>Fixed Medical Allowance (FMA for non-CGHS pensioners, if opted)</td>
              <td class="num" id="slipFma">₹1,000</td>
            </tr>
            <tr style="font-weight: 800; background: var(--accent-green-bg);">
              <td style="color: var(--accent-green);">Net Monthly Pension Disbursed to Bank</td>
              <td class="num" id="slipNetPension" style="color: var(--accent-green);">₹31,373</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

    </section>

    <!-- 1300+ WORDS COMPREHENSIVE SEO ARTICLE -->
    <article class="article-wrap">
      <h2>Understanding Pension Recalibration Under the 8th Central Pay Commission</h2>
      <p>
        For over 6.7 million retired Central Government personnel, defence veterans, railway pensioners, and surviving family dependents, the constitution of the <strong>8th Central Pay Commission (CPC)</strong> marks the most vital financial development in a decade. Over a pensioner's retirement lifespan, real income is constantly eroded by healthcare inflation, everyday commodity surges, and urban cost-of-living adjustments. 
      </p>
      <p>
        While active employees depend on pay revisions to elevate basic salary and allowances, retirees rely on Pay Commissions for structural recalibration of their core annuity: the <strong>Basic Pension</strong>. Unlike regular semi-annual Dearness Relief (DR) installments that merely counter temporary retail price index surges, a Central Pay Commission reconstructs the primary foundation of pension calculations, establishing complete parity between earlier retirees and newly retiring personnel.
      </p>

      <h2>1. The Foundation of Pension Parity: Modified Parity Principle Explained</h2>
      <p>
        A central pillar of the Indian civil and military pension system is the <strong>Principle of Modified Parity</strong>. In earlier decades, pensioners who retired under earlier Pay Commissions received lower pensions than colleagues retiring years later from the exact same post with the exact same service length. This created severe structural wage compression and retirement inequality.
      </p>
      <p>
        Starting from major rulings affirmed in the landmark <em>D.S. Nakara vs. Union of India</em> Supreme Court judgment, and subsequently codified in the 5th, 6th, and 7th CPCs, pension revision adheres to uniform consolidation rules:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Full Parity Linkage:</strong> Basic pension is pegged at precisely <strong>50% of the minimum basic pay</strong> in the revised Pay Matrix corresponding to the rank, post, or Pay Level from which the pensioner retired.</li>
        <li><strong>Consolidated Fitment Multiplication:</strong> For existing retirees, their current basic pension is updated directly using the approved <strong>fitment factor</strong>. If the resulting figure falls below 50% of the revised entry basic of that level in the new Pay Matrix, the pension is stepped up to meet the 50% floor automatically.</li>
        <li><strong>Dearness Relief (DR) Absorption:</strong> The accumulated Dearness Relief (which climbed past the 50% mark under 7th CPC guidelines) is folded completely into the newly consolidated basic pension. DR officially resets to <strong>0%</strong> on the implementation date.</li>
      </ul>

      <div class="formula-banner">
        Revised 8th CPC Basic Pension = Current 7th CPC Basic Pension × Approved Fitment Factor
      </div>

      <h2>2. Projecting the Fitment Multiplier: Fiscal Realities and Demands</h2>
      <p>
        The magnitude of pension increases hinges on the final fitment multiplier approved by the Union Cabinet. Pensioner associations, including the Bharat Pensioners Samaj (BPS) and the National Coordination Committee of Pensioners Associations (NCCPA), alongside active staff councils (JCM), have submitted detailed representations to the Department of Pension and Pensioners' Welfare (DoP&PW) and the Ministry of Finance.
      </p>

